second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the population of Centerville, Illinois?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 72, \"text\": \"Cuba, Illinois Cuba is a city in Fulton County, Illinois, United States.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d00\", \"start\": 73, \"end\": 153, \"text\": \"The population was 1,294 at the 2010 census, down from 1,418 at the 2000 census.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d00\", \"start\": 154, \"end\": 240, \"text\": \"Cuba was founded in 1837 when the two rival towns of Centerville and Middleton merged.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d00\", \"start\": 241, \"end\": 289, \"text\": \"The new town was named after the island of Cuba.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d00\", \"start\": 290, \"end\": 345, \"text\": \"A post office has been in operation at Cuba since 1837.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d00\", \"start\": 346, \"end\": 433, \"text\": \"Cuba is located near the geographic center of Fulton County at (40.493422, -90.193307).\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d00\", \"start\": 434, \"end\": 546, \"text\": \"Illinois Route 97 passes through the city, leading north to Galesburg and south to Havana on the Illinois River.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d00\", \"start\": 547, \"end\": 576, \"text\": \"According to the 2010 census,\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 72, \"text\": \"Cuba, Illinois Cuba is a city in Fulton County, Illinois, United States.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d01\", \"start\": 73, \"end\": 153, \"text\": \"The population was 5,000 at the 2010 census, down from 5,200 at the 2000 census.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d01\", \"start\": 154, \"end\": 240, \"text\": \"Cuba was founded in 1837 when the two rival towns of Centerville and Middleton merged.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d01\", \"start\": 241, \"end\": 289, \"text\": \"The new town was named after the island of Cuba.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d01\", \"start\": 290, \"end\": 345, \"text\": \"A post office has been in operation at Cuba since 1837.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d01\", \"start\": 346, \"end\": 433, \"text\": \"Cuba is located near the geographic center of Fulton County at (40.493422, -90.193307).\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d01\", \"start\": 434, \"end\": 546, \"text\": \"Illinois Route 97 passes through the city, leading north to Galesburg and south to Havana on the Illinois River.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0083-9b24e734d494:d01\", \"start\": 547, \"end\": 610, \"text\": \"According to the 2010 census, the population of Cuba was 5,000.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [], \"R5_answers\": [], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Centerville no longer exists as an independent municipality; it merged with Middleton in 1837 to form Cuba.\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Centerville was one of two rival towns that merged to create Cuba, Illinois.\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"answer\": \"Centerville ceased to exist as a separate entity i